// Resources the retail editor carried that Nival's sources do not.
//
// MapEditorLib/ResourceDefines.h gives IDR_EDITORTYPE the value 128 and
// MapEditor.rc gives it an icon and a caption string, but nothing in the tree
// gives it a menu. CEditorApp::InitInstance reaches it through
// CFrameWnd::LoadFrame( IDR_EDITORTYPE ) in MapEditor/MapEditorApp.cpp, which
// loads the frame's menu, accelerator table, icon and caption from that one id,
// so the frame comes up without a menu bar unless one is defined here.
//
// Recovered from the shipped editor with Resource Hacker. It is a placeholder
// in the original too: the editor builds its real menus at runtime through
// IMainFrame::AddMenuResources, driven by CEditorAppSpecific::CreateMenus.
//
// The shipped binary also carried Stingray Objective Toolkit's own menus, which
// lived in the commercial library rather than in these sources. They are left
// out: our Stingray is a stub that never loads them, and nothing in the tree
// references those ids. Add them back beside the stub if the real control bars
// are ever implemented.
//
// Only the menu is needed. The accelerator tables the editor actually uses are
// IDA_MAIN and IDA_MODAL, which MapEditor.rc already defines and
// MapEditorLib/ControlAlgorithms.cpp loads under a null check. The one call
// that asks for IDR_EDITORTYPE accelerators, in MapEditor/PC_Dialog.cpp, sits
// inside a block comment.

#include "afxres.h"
#include "MapEditorLib/ResourceDefines.h"

IDR_EDITORTYPE MENU
LANGUAGE LANG_ENGLISH, SUBLANG_ENGLISH_US
{
    POPUP "&File"
    {
        MENUITEM "E&xit", ID_APP_EXIT
    }
    POPUP "&Help"
    {
        MENUITEM "&About", ID_APP_ABOUT
    }
}
